{"uid":"include/js_policy.h::allowlist","name":"allowlist","qualname":"allowlist","kind":"function","file":"include/js_policy.h","line":34,"end_line":34,"language":"h","signature":"* allowlist (e.g. hb_is_allowlisted over js.conf). Fails closed: an unknown mode * yields false. */ bool jsp_enabled(jsp_mode mode, int host_allowlisted);","params":[{"name":"conf","annotation":"e.g. hb_is_allowlisted over js.","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"*","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"","description":"","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"include/js_policy.h","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":["include/js_policy.h::membership"]}
{"uid":"include/js_policy.h::jsp_trusted","name":"jsp_trusted","qualname":"jsp_trusted","kind":"function","file":"include/js_policy.h","line":45,"end_line":45,"language":"h","signature":"bool jsp_trusted(bool js_enabled, int host_allowlisted);","params":[{"name":"js_enabled","annotation":"bool","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"host_allowlisted","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"bool","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Trusted-host doctrine (Hito 28): a host the user declared trustworthy TWICE -- its JS is enabled (js_enabled, e.g. the jsp_enabled result) AND it is explicitly on allow.conf (host_allowlisted, e.g. hb_is_allowlisted over allow.conf) -- gets the full modern experience: author CSS and images on AND page-JS network access without per-session toggles.","description":"Either signal alone fails closed; a global JSP_ON without the allowlist entry is NOT trust. Reader mode is applied by the orchestrator afterwards and wins.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"include/js_policy.h","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"include/js_policy.h::jsp_present_trusted","name":"jsp_present_trusted","qualname":"jsp_present_trusted","kind":"function","file":"include/js_policy.h","line":54,"end_line":54,"language":"h","signature":"bool jsp_present_trusted(int host_allowlisted);","params":[{"name":"host_allowlisted","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"bool","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Presentation-trust (2026-07-11): a host EXPLICITLY on allow.conf (host_allowlisted, e.g. hb_is_allowlisted over allow.conf) gets author PRESENTATION -- author CSS and <img> images -- without per-session toggles, independent of JS.","description":"Rationale: putting a host in allow.conf is an explicit statement of trust in that site; presentation (colours, borders, gradients, images) is strictly lower risk than script/network, which stay DOUBLE-gated on allow.conf AND js.conf via jsp_trusted. Fails closed for a non-allowlisted host (host_allowlisted == 0). Reader mode wins over this too.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"include/js_policy.h","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
